Remove finished sounds from their voice so voices end with their sounds

main's af4dc22 taught the daemon to prune the voice manager: a periodic
task removed each finished sample from its voice and dropped empty
voices. v2.1's restructured command loop lost that when main was merged
in, and nothing in v2.1 calls VoiceManager::remove_sample or
cleanup_empty_voices. Every play therefore left a permanent entry (each
play without a voice added a whole new auto voice), /status/voices
listed voices whose sounds had ended, voice_stop and voice_fade_out on
such a voice reported success for sample ids that no longer existed,
and a later play into a reused voice name silently inherited the old
voice_volume.

The reaper already reconciles every finished sample and streamed source
through reconcile_finished_voice, so that is where the voice manager is
now pruned: the finished id leaves its voice, and VoiceManager's
remove_sample drops the voice once it is empty. Voice commands on a
voice whose sounds have all finished now report "not found", as they do
on main, and a voice played again starts at full volume.

Tests (written first, each failing for the reason above): a finished
sample leaves its voice while its sibling stays, and the voice goes with
its last sample; a finished streamed source leaves its voice;
voice_stop, voice_fade_out and voice_volume on an ended voice warn "not
found" and send nothing to the audio thread; a voice played again after
it ended starts at volume 1.0.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
and a warning-free release build (RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings); fuzz suite 7
passed; broker-backed native suite (MQTTAUDIO_BROKER_TESTS=1, TLS CA
set) 945 passed, 0 failed, 7 device-gated ignored.

